cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Drishti-PAM — Hybrid Structural-Deviation Detection for Privileged-Access Monitoring"
message: "If you use this software in academic or industrial work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-SURNAME"
    given-names: "REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-FIRST-NAME"
abstract: >
  A reproducible, two-detector pipeline for catching insider-risk behaviour in
  Privileged Access Management (PAM) session telemetry. A deterministic rule
  baseline runs alongside a hybrid LLM classifier (DistilBERT text encoder + a
  categorical MLP, late fusion, focal loss with class-weighted sampling); both
  detectors are evaluated on the same held-out split so their numbers are
  directly comparable. Includes a synthetic data generator covering twelve
  insider-risk scenarios plus one adversarial vocabulary-cloak control (S16),
  three SOAR/SIEM integration sketches (Splunk SPL, Microsoft Sentinel KQL,
  Cortex XSOAR playbook), a multi-stage Dockerfile that packages the static
  dashboard, and a two-tier dashboard (headline hero + operator triage
  console) that surfaces every model decision against per-session ground
  truth.
repository-code: "https://github.com/camseye/drishti-pam"
